WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:05.050
<v Speaker 1>Welcome to the award ceremony for Pro Tour Venice.</v>

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:20.610
<v Speaker 1>Today we're here to salute the top players in our game. But first let's have a salute for all the volunteers, staff and judges who made this event possible. Thank you.</v>

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:34.370
<v Speaker 1>First, I'd like to call up the finalist of the team Masters</v>

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.240
<v Speaker 1>three young gentlemen from Canada by the names of Stephen Wolfman, Elijah Pollock and David Rude. Come on up, guys.</v>

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:09.140
<v Speaker 1>For their performance this weekend, these gentlemen will be taking home $30,000. Congratulations.</v>

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:25.660
<v Speaker 1>And now the Champs</v>

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.860
<v Speaker 1>from Japan</v>

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:32.860
<v Speaker 1>Team PS2, Mashiro Kuroda,</v>

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.820
<v Speaker 1>Katsuhiro Mori</v>

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:37.300
<v Speaker 1>and Mashiko Marita.</v>

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:13.560
<v Speaker 1>In addition to fame and glory as Masters champion, this team will be taking home $60,000. Congratulations.</v>

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:30.440
<v Speaker 1>And now we turn to the Champions of Pro Tour Venice.</v>

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:33.760
<v Speaker 1>I'll call up the top 4 competitors</v>

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:38.640
<v Speaker 1>1st from College Park, MD William Jensen.</v>

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:55.580
<v Speaker 1>He's still a little rusty.</v>

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:02.210
<v Speaker 1>Mr. Johnson will be taking home $13,000. Congratulations, William.</v>

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:09.700
<v Speaker 1>Next gentleman is from Philly,</v>

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:14.810
<v Speaker 1>Philadelphia, PA, United States. Jordan Berkowitz.</v>

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:28.970
<v Speaker 1>He's a little shy,</v>

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:32.640
<v Speaker 1>but $15,000 should help that. Congratulations.</v>

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:39.830
<v Speaker 1>And now</v>

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.970
<v Speaker 1>from Americold Finland, Tommy Wallabies.</v>

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:07.220
<v Speaker 1>And finally, the champion of Pro Tour Venice</v>

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:12.580
<v Speaker 1>from Union, NJ. Please give a huge hand to OSA Libido Wiz.</v>

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:29.130
<v Speaker 1>Between OSU and the splits he assuredly has with his team,</v>

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:33.850
<v Speaker 1>they'll be taking home $30,000. Congratulations, Joseph.</v>

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:42.310
<v Speaker 1>And let's have all the top 4 Pro Tour players up here.</v>

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:59.100
<v Speaker 1>$78,000 in winnings right here. Good job guys,</v>

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:02.250
<v Speaker 1>and let's have the top 2 Masters teams,</v>

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:10.780
<v Speaker 1>$90,000 in winnings coming up here. If anyone needs dinner tonight,</v>

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.120
<v Speaker 1>I'll look at that.</v>

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.610
<v Speaker 1>And thanks to everyone. We'll see you for our Pro Tour Yokohama next. Have a good night.</v>

